A worker finishes its running job on SIGTERM

Why: StartWorkerShell installs no signal handler, so SIGTERM ends the worker at once and its running job stays at status 0. With the handler the worker takes no new job and exits once the running one ends; the supervisor (files/misp_container/worker.py) waits WORKER_STOP_GRACE for it.
Upstream: not filed yet

